Fish Fillets
https://github.com/wenhuanli/FishFillets.git


Compile requirements
====================

CMake >= 3.16, www.cmake.org

Library SDL3 = Simple DirectMedia Layer (video, input, sound)
- libSDL3, www.libsdl.org

Library SDL3_mixer (multiple sounds)
- libSDL3_mixer, https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer

Library SDL3_image (PNG support)
- libSDL3_image, https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_image

Library SDL3_ttf (TrueType UTF-8 fonts)
- libSDL3_ttf, https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_ttf

Library LUA (script language, used for debug console, configuration, levels,...)
- lua >= 5.5, www.lua.org

Library FriBidi (optional, bidirectional text support)
- libfribidi, https://github.com/fribidi/fribidi


How to run
==========

I. Compile
----------

- Compile the game:
$ git clone https://github.com/wenhuanli/FishFillets.git
$ cd FishFillets
$ cmake -S . -B build
$ cmake --build build
$ cmake --install build

II. Install data
----------------

- Download fillets-ng-data from http://fillets.sourceforge.net/download.php
- Extract fillets-ng-data.tar.gz to a $datadir.
  default: /usr/local/share/games/fillets/

III. Run it
-----------
$ ./build/src/game/fillets systemdir=$datadir

Controls
========

Up, down, left and right arrow keys control the current fish.
Use space bar to switch between the fish.

See also "How to Play" $datadir/doc/html/manual.html

restart level - Backspace
undo - -/+
help - F1
save game - F2
load game - F3
show/hide move counter - F5
show/hide subtitles - F6
game menu - F10
fullscreen - F11
faster game - Shift
